\section{N-Body Gravity on Tetrahedral Mass Distribution}

Let \(\rho(\mathbf{x})\) be mass density defined over the tetrahedral complex \(\mathcal{T}\).
The gravitational interaction at position \(\mathbf{x}_i\) is
\[
\mathbf{F}(\mathbf{x}_i)
=
- G \int_V \int_V
\frac{\rho(\mathbf{x}_i)\rho(\mathbf{x}_j)}{\lVert \mathbf{x}_i - \mathbf{x}_j \rVert^2}
\hat{\mathbf{r}}_{ij}
\, dV_i \, dV_j,
\]
where
\[
\hat{\mathbf{r}}_{ij} = \frac{\mathbf{x}_i - \mathbf{x}_j}{\lVert \mathbf{x}_i - \mathbf{x}_j \rVert}.
\]

In the discrete tetrahedral setting,
\[
\mathbf{F}(\mathbf{x}_i)
\approx
- G \sum_{j}
\frac{m_i m_j}{\lVert \mathbf{x}_i - \mathbf{x}_j \rVert^2}
\hat{\mathbf{r}}_{ij},
\]
with \(m_i = \int_{T_i} \rho(\mathbf{x})\, dV\).